== (d) Q mod 2 and the Fibonacci leapers ==
Q mod 2 on the nonzero classes: (1, 0) -> (0, 1) -> (1, 1) -> (1, 0) ; order of Q mod 2: 3
  n= 0 Q^n(0,1) = (  0,  1) rook/wazir   mod 2 = (0, 1)  colour-preserving: False  n = 1 mod 3: False
  n= 1 Q^n(0,1) = (  1,  1) bishop/ferz  mod 2 = (1, 1)  colour-preserving: True   n = 1 mod 3: True
  n= 2 Q^n(0,1) = (  1,  2) knight       mod 2 = (1, 0)  colour-preserving: False  n = 1 mod 3: False
  n= 3 Q^n(0,1) = (  2,  3) zebra        mod 2 = (0, 1)  colour-preserving: False  n = 1 mod 3: False
  n= 4 Q^n(0,1) = (  3,  5)              mod 2 = (1, 1)  colour-preserving: True   n = 1 mod 3: True
  n= 5 Q^n(0,1) = (  5,  8)              mod 2 = (1, 0)  colour-preserving: False  n = 1 mod 3: False
  n= 6 Q^n(0,1) = (  8, 13)              mod 2 = (0, 1)  colour-preserving: False  n = 1 mod 3: False
  n= 7 Q^n(0,1) = ( 13, 21)              mod 2 = (1, 1)  colour-preserving: True   n = 1 mod 3: True
  n= 8 Q^n(0,1) = ( 21, 34)              mod 2 = (1, 0)  colour-preserving: False  n = 1 mod 3: False
  n= 9 Q^n(0,1) = ( 34, 55)              mod 2 = (0, 1)  colour-preserving: False  n = 1 mod 3: False
  n=10 Q^n(0,1) = ( 55, 89)              mod 2 = (1, 1)  colour-preserving: True   n = 1 mod 3: True
  n=11 Q^n(0,1) = ( 89,144)              mod 2 = (1, 0)  colour-preserving: False  n = 1 mod 3: False
  n=12 Q^n(0,1) = (144,233)              mod 2 = (0, 1)  colour-preserving: False  n = 1 mod 3: False
Q^3 = ((1, 2), (2, 3)) (columns: knight (1,2), zebra (2,3));  -Q^3 mod 2 = ((1, 0), (0, 1)) = I
